================ A3: re-reading v2's own query for dataset constraints ================

-- v2 script lines that query the monthly table for P_F/TA_F --
[1] "mo_era5 <- dbGetQuery(con, \"SELECT site_id, TIMESTAMP, P_ERA FROM monthly WHERE dataset = 'ERA5'\")"            
[2] "mo_fluxmet <- dbGetQuery(con, \"SELECT site_id, TIMESTAMP, P_F, P_F_QC FROM monthly WHERE dataset = 'FLUXMET'\")"
[3] "mo_fluxmet <- mo_fluxmet |> dplyr::mutate(TIMESTAMP = as.Date(TIMESTAMP), year = lubridate::year(TIMESTAMP),"    
[4] "pf_all <- mo_fluxmet |> dplyr::filter(year >= KG_ERA5_PERIOD[1], year <= KG_ERA5_PERIOD[2]) |>"                  
[5] "pf_qc0 <- mo_fluxmet |> dplyr::filter(year >= KG_ERA5_PERIOD[1], year <= KG_ERA5_PERIOD[2], P_F_QC == 0) |>"     
[6] "n_months_total <- mo_fluxmet |> dplyr::filter(year >= KG_ERA5_PERIOD[1], year <= KG_ERA5_PERIOD[2]) |>"          
[7] "  mo_fluxmet |> dplyr::filter(year >= KG_ERA5_PERIOD[1], year <= KG_ERA5_PERIOD[2], P_F_QC == 0) |>"             

================ A4: P_F_QC polarity verification (root cause) ================

-- Network-wide (n= 74916 site-months): fraction identical to P_ERA, by P_F_QC bin --
      qc_bin     n frac_identical_to_era5
1    [0,0.1] 22546             0.98567373
2  (0.1,0.2]   404             0.05693069
3  (0.2,0.3]   417             0.04316547
4  (0.3,0.4]   380             0.02368421
5  (0.4,0.5]   735             0.01768707
6  (0.5,0.6]   498             0.01606426
7  (0.6,0.7]   635             0.01732283
8  (0.7,0.8]   877             0.01026226
9  (0.8,0.9]  1368             0.01023392
10   (0.9,1] 47056             0.00750170

P_F_QC == 0 exactly: n= 22101  frac identical to P_ERA = 1 
P_F_QC == 1 exactly: n= 38205  frac identical to P_ERA = 0.007930899 

CONCLUSION: P_F_QC=0 means ENTIRELY GAP-FILLED (from ERA5); P_F_QC=1 means ENTIRELY
 MEASURED (independent) -- the OPPOSITE polarity from the raw HH-resolution System-2
 convention (0=measured) that v2 applied uncritically to this MM-resolution FRACTION
 field. v2's 'P_F_QC=0 = fully measured' filter selected exactly the wrong months --
 the ones guaranteed to be identical to P_ERA by construction. This is the actual
 root cause of v2's flagged identity: neither ingestion collision (A2 finds none) nor
 an unconstrained query (A3 finds the query was correctly constrained), but an analyst
 misreading of an ambiguously-documented, resolution-dependent QC convention.
Saved: review/diagnostics/era5_precip_units_v3/table_a4_qc_polarity.csv

